{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeBreadthFirstSearchEvent"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edge"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","text":"Hashable"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each source is discovered first. Then, for each vertex in the order discovered, its out-edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are reported as tree edges (to an undiscovered vertex, which is then discovered) or non-tree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges (to a discovered one); then the vertex is finished. In a directed graph every out-edge of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an explored vertex is reported. In an undirected graph each edge is reported once, from the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"end whose edges are examined first: the tree edge is not reported again from the vertex it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"discovered, but a parallel edge to the parent is a non-tree edge, and a self-loop is one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"non-tree edge."}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Traversal\/documentation\/Traversal